    "notes": "Closed score with German labels \"Sopran/Alt\" and \"Tenor/Bass\" (abbreviated \"S./A.\", \"T./B.\" on later systems). Split each staff by stem direction into four parts. There is one lyric line under EACH staff: the upper line belongs to the Sopran, except mm.9-10 where the Sopran has whole-bar rests and the same line carries the Alt echo \"an uns und allen Enden\"; the lower line belongs to the Bass, except mm.9-10 where the Bass rests and the line belongs to the Tenor. In m.3 the Bass sings a dotted rhythm, so its syllable \"Her-\" sits half a beat after the Sopran's. A correct conversion attaches each syllable to the voice whose note it is printed under (truth: Sopran mm.1-8,11-12; Alt mm.9-10; Bass mm.1-8,11-12; Tenor mm.9-10)."
  },
